"""estate-cutover-readers (goal.md): every shelf reader tolerates estate-cutover's estate_cutover rows.

A fixture state root with representative rows on every shelf is cut over dev -> workstation by the real ops/bin/estate-cutover.
Its twin is the same root with only the estate_cutover rows removed (the pre-cutover shelves under the same record).
Every reader op, script and helper runs against both, from its own copy of the code; each must exit without a
traceback and print the same thing on both, and the shelves the readers append to must end with the same rows.

  check                     the fixture root (scripts/check; temp dirs only)
  check --state-copy DIR    a COPY of a real state root (never ~/.contextstack itself); copied again, never written
"""
